    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36663" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξαλλοτρι-όω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>export,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Str.
				5.1.9
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>divert, alienate,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόρον εἰς ἑτέρας χρείας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>BSA</u>
					17.229
				</span></i>
			 (Pamphyl.), cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>PGiss.</u>
				2.24
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii B. C.)</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>alienate, estrange,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸν πολιτικὸν ὄχλον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.H.
					11.39
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοὺς πολλοὺς πρὸς τοὺς ἀρίστους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.E.
					<u>M.</u>
					2.42
				</span></i>
			:—
				Pass.
			, <i>to be estranged,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>1 Ma.</u>
				12.10
			</span></i>.</div>
